millions of people in Shanghai counted  down to midnight on Wednesday  celebrating the end of a strict  two-month pandemic lockdown  there were scenes of joy and excitement  as people socialized outdoors and drove  their cars for the first time in weeks  Street barricades have been removed  supermarkets restaurants and parks are  reopening public transport has resumed  China's biggest city and Commercial  Center is slowly coming back to life  after being shut down at the end of  March  more than 600 000 coronavirus infections  were recorded in what was the country's  worst outbreak since the pandemic began  artist Sunshine was visiting the city  and became stuck in his hotel an initial  five-day lockdown stretched to more than  60 days  he's relieved it's over but remains  distrustful of the government  order so they tell people only five days  so I think you're fine but you know the  government always lie two people  the more and more and the more longer  and the longer and the longer and no  ending no people when it's finished  there was widespread anger along with  confusion over food shortages and a lack  of access to Emergency Medical Care the  lockdown also crippled Supply chains and  slowed the economy property and Car  Sales the service sector and Retail  consumption all plummeted in April  analysts say recovery won't be quick or  easy after the initial phase there might  be more disappointments  um because the reality is the consumer  confidence is dampened a property Market  is still weak although the weakness in  other parts of the economy was still  there and not addressed and on top of  that income growth has slowed  significantly so after the lift of all  the restrictions I think there is a lot  of work has to to be done  Shanghai authorities say the city has  achieved a mile start in its battle  against the virus in a letter they  thanked residents for their patience and  apologized for the inconveniences caused  people in Shanghai may be celebrating  for now but the memory of this long  lockdown won't easily be forgotten  China's leaders refused to live with the  coronavirus and any new outbreak can  result in the lives of millions being  upended without notice  Katrina you Al Jazeera Beijing
 

